Significance: minor
Type: added

Added recurrence to the calendar export. A recurring series now describes its whole schedule in one `.ics` component carrying an `RRULE`, with any canceled dates listed as `EXDATE` exclusions, so subscribing once gets every date and keeps getting them. Downloading a single date gives a component carrying the series identifier and a `RECURRENCE-ID` naming that date, which is what tells a calendar client it is looking at one instance of a series rather than a separate event. Recurring series also appear once each in the site-wide, archive, venue and taxonomy feeds. This changes the emitted start for every event with a named timezone, recurring or not: where the feed previously emitted `DTSTART:20300615T183000Z`, a bare UTC instant, it now emits `DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20300615T143000`. A repeat rule cannot be attached correctly to a UTC-anchored start, because "every Tuesday at 18:30" is a claim about the wall clock and a UTC anchor drifts an hour at each daylight saving change. Every calendar now also carries a `VTIMEZONE` definition for each timezone its events name, which is what RFC 5545 requires of a `TZID` and what keeps the new start valid. An event whose timezone is a fixed UTC offset is unchanged and keeps the bare UTC form.
